e combos | ✅ 6/6 (3 combos × dev/release) |\n\n## Two real issues found and fixed (both in my harness, not the library)\n\n1. **Stale-artifact blind spot.** `cargo test` never rebuilds a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` target, so loading `target/release/*.so` opportunistically tests an old binary. I proved this by injecting a bug into the `default:` arm — **all 28 tests still passed**. The harness now shells out to `cargo build --release --lib` into a dedicated `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`; the same injected bug was then caught by 10 rows. Control reverted; `src/lib.rs` is byte-intact.\n2. `to_bits() - 1` ULP stepping underflowed at `h == 0.0` (dev-profile-only panic) — replaced with `next_down`/`next_up`.\n\n## Notable C behaviors confirmed replicated\n- `(int)floorf(h/60)` on NaN/±Inf/overflow → x86-64 `cvttss2si` yields `INT_MIN`, selecting the `default:` arm, **not** `case 0`. Verified against C built at `-O0` (libm `floorf` call) and `-O2`/`-O3` (inlined `roundss`) — all match.\n- `s == -0.0f` takes the early return (C `-0.0f == 0` is true); `s = NaN`/subnormal do not.\n- No `NULL` check exists in C; both libraries fault with `SIGSEGV` identically (asserted out-of-process so the harness survives). A Rust-side null check would have been a divergence.\n- Aliasing (`dest == src`, ±1/±2 offsets), unaligned pointers, and exactly-3-reads/3-writes canaries all match.\n\nArtifacts in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/{common/mod.rs,phase_b_configs.rs,phase_c_errors.rs}`, plus `check_parity.sh` and `run_all.sh` to reproduce. `c_src/` was not modified (the alternate-`-O` builds went to `$TMPDIR`).","ttft_ms":2541,"type":"result","duration_ms":620855,"uuid":"bf4f6422-a430-4dd1-9bc5-1a04ff97f6c2","ttft_stream_ms":2355,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":2356,"queued_turn_count":0}
